{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide","id":1079624,"title":"Beast Storyteller's Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-16T19:05:40-07:00","id":1079624,"title":"Beast Storyteller's Guide","content":"So, let's say that the next book I was going to outline was the <b>Beast STG</b>. What sorts of things would you find useful in such a book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:17:48-07:00","id":1079630,"title":"","content":"Incarnate Lore and more story hooks for them would be pretty great<br /> American guide about finding old Lairs and conquering them<br /> a guide to make battles against heroes more complex affairs<br /> More creatures from the primordial dream that ate related to beasts but not beasts.<br /> perhaps some kind of covenant for beasts, a huge organization with a common goal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:26:38-07:00","id":1079633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide#post1079624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's say that the next book I was going to outline was the <b>Beast STG</b>. What sorts of things would you find useful in such a book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting Shards. They let one play with various facets and concepts without having to worry too much about affect the &quot;proper&quot; setting.<br /> More cross-over support. Not that it is particularly lacking, but as &quot;the Cross-over splat&quot; more mechanics and advice about integrating the other supernaturals (and their supporting Themes) into Beast would always help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:41:21-07:00","id":1079640,"title":"","content":"It depends on what's in the Player's Guide, to be honest. I think most of what I want to see is likely to be in that book, but since you asked...<br /> <br /> More information about Hives and how they work, more information on the Primordial Dream and how it fits into the Astral (I fucking love the Astral), maybe something to play up the territoriality of Beasts, I'd definitely like to see how Beasts fit into the themes of other supernaturals as well, some advice on how to portray Heroes as villains (like maybe they tend to get their groupies killed in a blaze of glory or something -- relatively mundane stuff that makes them assholes, you know?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T19:51:31-07:00","id":1079642,"title":"","content":"More information on what beasts do narrative wise. I've struggled to understand what beasts actually do in games aside from feed and deal with heroes, so help in that area would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:07:00-07:00","id":1079672,"title":"","content":"More, even non-canon, parts of <b>Beasts</b> society. Basic <b>BtP</b> is low on their own lore to make them jive in crossovers, but what about us wanting to run a rather strict Begotten games? Some new society variants would be great.<br /> <br /> Examples scenarios to run, like those in <b>Werewolf the Forsaken </b>2E corebook. Nothing more than 2-3 pages, but springing and highlighting some specifics of <b>Beast</b> gameline as story inspirations.<br /> <br /> And when we are at this - Brood creation rules, similar to <b>WtF Pack</b> creation. Beasts broods maybe are not so extensive as packs, but idea how to connect different beasts would be golden!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:11:02-07:00","id":1079675,"title":"","content":"Plot seeds that make the legends of the Dark Mother actively relevant in-game. Bonus points these also provide crossover hooks.<br /> <br /> More on Hive politics and social structure.<br /> <br /> Beast relations with non-player &quot;Family&quot; (Strix, Shartha, Gentry, Simulatai, etc etc)<br /> <br /> Alternate setting Shards, including possibly appropriate rule hacks<br /> <br /> Primordial Dream phenomena to explore/harness/be threatened by/etc<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (This is assuming a Players Guide is also doable. Because if not, throw in more Nightmares [especially Kinship ones] and Atavisms, and any new Families or Hungers you may have planned)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T23:31:57-07:00","id":1079696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1079675#post1079675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This is assuming a Players Guide is also doable. Because if not, throw in more Nightmares [especially Kinship ones] and Atavisms, and any new Families or Hungers you may have planned)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Player's Guide is currently in development, which is the step before it goes into editing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T07:40:41-07:00","id":1079785,"title":"","content":"We had a thread like for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848254-beast-player-s-guide-suggestions-requests\">Player's Guide</a> in fact.<br /> <br /> Something posted in it by YeOfLittleFaith that I thought would make better ST Guide material, so will repost here, was:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really want to see more on the Primordial Dream as an environment and ecosystem and specific instances of the impact it can have on the world in addition to Beasts and Heroes. A deeper look at how both deal with the Dream and the relationship of the Begotten to the rest of the Astral would be great. Also, if there's room for it, more on dreamers. What happens to a proto-Beast who <i>refuses</i> her own primordial self? How does the experience of Beasts-to-be with it differ from dormant Heroes or from Beasts who, for some odd reason or tragic twist, never come to be? Are there <i>other dreamers </i>still in these modern times where the lessons of fear are drowned by the bluster of numberless humans? </div> </div> </div><br /> Some discussion of the non-&quot;all Beasts must die and I get to be the awesome who kills them&quot; type of Hero (perhaps the comparison between the two culd parallel the that between regular Beasts and Insatiables).<br /> <br /> Some Dread Systems for building supernatural family and other phenomena. Beasts might be the crossover critters, but that side of the game shouldn't <i>have</i> to require books from outside the line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide#post1079624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's say that the next book I was going to outline was the <b>Beast STG</b>. What sorts of things would you find useful in such a book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm faintly amused by the fact that you phrased this so it's possible to interpret it as it <i>not</i> being the next the thing you're woking on, and you just fucking with us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 04-18-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:54:13-07:00","id":1079815,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely like to see some setting shards and hacks that give other ways to run the game. Families as actual bloodlines passed down from generation to generation, Heroes that fulfill their original purpose in the Primordial Dream, Horrors with agendas of their own that don't necessarily relate directly to their immediate Hunger. Heck, while I've never been that bothered by the rarity of physical transformation, I know that there's a lot of people who were, so a hack for that could fit into a shard easily enough.<br /> Assuming it isn't already covered in the Player's Guide, I'd like to see more information on Hives and the effects that the Apex has on one. <br /> I'd like to see more on the Primordial Dream. I know there's some of that in the Player's Guide, but until I see that, I'm just going to have to assume that there can never be too much on that. I'd especially like to see some weirdness related to the Primordial Dream that baffles even Beasts.<br /> I'm seconding the request for information on how Beasts relate to the more alien creatures lurking in the world.<br /> Antagonists that aren't Kin that also aren't linked to the God Machine could be an interesting addition. That could be either a new type of critter, or an odd occurrence with existing ones.<br /> White Oak Dragon as one of the writers. I think that one might be personal bias, though, and probably doesn't reflect the desires of the others. I'll just go get back to work now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That's what I came up with off the top of my head. If I come up with any more thoughts, I'll be back to suggest them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:50:55-07:00","id":1079906,"title":"","content":"Something I really liked in the Demon STG was the additional crunch for angel NPCs; I think Heroes could use some extra stuff in their arsenal, too, and maybe even some alternate rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:15:48-07:00","id":1079924,"title":"","content":"More settings to show off the new rules that get introduced and the themes discussed. That was one of my favourite parts of The Pack, and I would love to see it here too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:01:27-07:00","id":1079978,"title":"","content":"Advice on running both &quot;Beast-only&quot; games, and crossover heavy games.<br /> More on the Primordial Dream and their creatures.<br /> New Hero powers by the gajillion.<br /> <br /> (Also, thank you so much for all your work Matt. I've been re-reading the core book and it's so good. Beast is now my favorite CoD line - and Promethean is just behind, so, you know, double thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","user":"Daigotsu Max","date":". 04-17-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:32:05-07:00","id":1079999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1079642#post1079642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More information on what beasts do narrative wise. I've struggled to understand what beasts actually do in games aside from feed and deal with heroes, so help in that area would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, this is how I feel about Vampire, too. Like, what do I actually do with this game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:39:41-07:00","id":1080382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1079785#post1079785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm faintly amused by the fact that you phrased this so it's possible to interpret it as it <i>not</i> being the next the thing you're woking on, and you just fucking with us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like something I'd do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No, really, there are a couple of projects that I <i>could</i> outline next, but I'm waiting to hear from OPP about a couple of them, so I figured I'd get some ideas from folks in the meanwhile. Every time we announce a book, someone on the forums says &quot;Oh, I hope it includes [something awesome],&quot; and then I'm like &quot;balls, I didn't think of that,&quot; so I figured I'd try and head that off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T10:11:52-07:00","id":1080403,"title":"","content":"What I quoted from YeOfLittleFaith is what I want most of all.<br /> <br /> Back when the game had more of a focus on othering as a theme, I suggested analogues of Heroes for other forms of othering than that outright violence. Like fetishisation - people who are fascinated by Beasts, and want seduce/tame/redeem them, live in Lairs, that sort of thing - people who might seem like they'd be easy to make into servants (and some of them might even think that's what's happening and welcome it), but actually put their own narrative chains on Beasts the way Heroes lay anathema. Or appropriation - people who form cults around the Dark Mother ajnd Primordial Dream - either wanting to become Beasts (whether that's possible or not) - or forcibly fitting Beasts into the structures of their own mythologies, again by narrative chains. The latter could be a subset of the former - &quot;I want you to be my face of divinity, so that's what you're going to be, whether you like it or not.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:24:34-07:00","id":1080449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1079672#post1079672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More, even non-canon, parts of <b>Beasts</b> society. Basic <b>BtP</b> is low on their own lore to make them jive in crossovers, but what about us wanting to run a rather strict Begotten games? Some new society variants would be great.<br /> <br /> Examples scenarios to run, like those in <b>Werewolf the Forsaken </b>2E corebook. Nothing more than 2-3 pages, but springing and highlighting some specifics of <b>Beast</b> gameline as story inspirations.<br /> <br /> And when we are at this - Brood creation rules, similar to <b>WtF Pack</b> creation. Beasts broods maybe are not so extensive as packs, but idea how to connect different beasts would be golden!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually agree with this a lot. I love the crossover information in the Core book, however, I do want to run some strictly Beast games and agree that it seems more initially designed to be crossover first and strict Beast games last.<br /> <br /> Brood creation rules woudl definitely be awesome too. We have Pack creation, Krewe creation, etc. so this would continue that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:00:58-07:00","id":1080469,"title":"","content":"It might have been Player's Guide material, but I'm going to link to a previous post of mine. It seemed to have been positively received:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912712#post912712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including Mortal relationships could enhance the contrast between the Life and Legend of the Beast, giving each its unique flavor. Also, the Beast attempting to reconcile its new nature with their old life allows for many intense stories. Being rejected or accepted by their human family would shape the Beast's character and inform their relationship with the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912563-waking-nightmares-or-on-the-nature-and-process-of-becoming-begotten?p=912712#post912712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that Chambers should be generated by all Integrity loss, not just that caused by the supernatural. Beasts would feel attracted to places representing the worst humanity has to offer, which is excellent story material. It even enhances the present Lesson-teaching philosophy, by pointing out where the Beast might want to get involved. More than that, I think it's an organic way to make even amoral Beasts look better. &quot;Sure&quot; a Beast says, &quot;I'm an abomination, but the world that allows this to happen can also have a place for me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rule hack: Beasts are bizarro-Prometheans. Instead of Elpis and the Principle they have Hunger and the Narrative, that drive the Beast to self-destruction. Unless they resist, they will ruin everything they love and seal their own doom while learning nothing. However, if the Beast grasps at personal development, strives to understand the consequences of their actions, and adopts a code of conduct, there is still hope. They might save what they care about, have their deaths have meaning and maybe even attain their New Dawn - finding balance with the world and forcing the Narrative to accept them. Such a hack would welcome Refinement-inspired philosophy splats.<br /> <br /> Refinement-inspired philosophy splats, would have been great regardless of everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T12:59:27-07:00","id":1080505,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see more exploration of the Primordial Dream, the Hive, and the Narrative that enchains both Beasts and Heroes. Although, speaking of Heroes I'd love to see a little more exploration of the Heroic condition that was teased at in Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes and maybe a few new Gifts for victorious Heroes to claim as their own. Noted: I am one of the minority who absolutely love the way Heroes are written up now (both mechanically and thematically) and encourage further development on that...with the exceptions being included as well (don't think I didn't notice the Integrity 5, 6, and face punching 7 included into Conquering Heroes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T20:28:10-07:00","id":1088610,"title":"","content":"The weird, shitty relations of Beasts. Not the other player splats, but things like how Beasts related to Haunted Houses, the Mothmen, the Men in Black, and the Black Eyed Children. Unique categories of monsters like the antagonists from the Demon Storyteller's Guide. Actually, a similar crossover section full of system hacks and plot hooks might note be a bad idea either. <br /> <br /> And I'd second a section on how Beasts relate to things like Strix, Huntsmen, and Amkhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:29:05-07:00","id":1088680,"title":"","content":"I would definitely like more variant heroes- some kind of upgrade/higher-level splat would go a long way to making them more threatening, as would new gifts. Maybe something on the &quot;nice&quot; heroes mentioned in the core book and what they do with their time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T11:49:34-07:00","id":1088808,"title":"","content":"1) More hungers<br /> 2) more developed Beast politics<br /> 3) More on fleshing out the Primordial Dream with non-lair settings and non-Horror creatures<br /> 4) Lots of possible origins/explanations for Beasts and their kinships<br /> 5) More crunch on developing Kinship Nightmares<br /> 6) Advice on roleplaying kinship with solipsistic/plain evil monsters like Strix, Slashers and Gentry<br /> 7) More Incarnate powers<br /> 8) More Hero Gifts<br /> 9) Beast Cults (I know they are in there)<br /> 10) Beast-related Minor Template<br /> 11) Hero-related Minor Template<br /> 12) More Primordial Dream phenomena<br /> 13) Advice on differentiating the Primordial Dream from Changeling dream worlds, the Hedge, the Astral, etc.<br /> 14) More on the Unfettered and the Rampant<br /> 15) A setting shard which gives Beasts an actual Integrity-equivalent<br /> 16) Setting shard where Heroes actually fulfill their role<br /> <br /> <br /> I know some of these were said earlier in the thread, but I want them too so I'll say them anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-06-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T19:28:55-07:00","id":1090092,"title":"","content":"More pre-made Atavisms and Nightmares.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe a section detailing monsters from various mythologies and how they might draw inspiration / parallels to the different families and hungers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T19:43:15-07:00","id":1090560,"title":"","content":"1.Info on how Beasts react to or interact with the God-Machine.<br /> 2.Rules for Heroes that follow the old-school &quot;spread the lesson&quot; model, rather than the &quot;It's my story and you're just set dressing!&quot; type.<br /> 3.What are the children of Beasts like?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 05-09-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:00:36-07:00","id":1095231,"title":"","content":"I add my vote to the requests for additional options for Heroes and expanded setting for the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> One thing I would like to see is some discussion of what happens if a Beast tries to change their Legend. We know Hungers can change, and a Beast's powers and identity are at least somewhat reciprocally based on the collective subconscious of the mortals they interact with, so what happens when a Beast decides &quot;I want to be more Batman than Jason, hockey masked Horror be damned&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T07:27:31-07:00","id":1098758,"title":"","content":"I'm still in the process of reading the book but have a Beast in my game. And to be honest there are so many holes in this book and so many incomplete and vague things in it. Anything you add in a players or storyteller book would only improve it. What do I want??? An index to the core book. Could we do that? No. Really. That would be the first step in the right direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T07:31:35-07:00","id":1098759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1098758#post1098758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still in the process of reading the book but have a Beast in my game. And to be honest there are so many holes in this book and so many incomplete and vague things in it. Anything you add in a players or storyteller book would only improve it. What do I want??? An index to the core book. Could we do that? No. Really. That would be the first step in the right direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The core book <i>has</i> an index. <br /> <br /> I'm probably going to regret asking this, but what the hell. What in the core book do you think is vague, incomplete, or full of holes?","signature":"","ed