:0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:42:47-07:00","id":1099369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1099106#post1099106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be neat to see ideas for things which can disturb the primordial dream other than Horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, i forgot about that. It should be on my list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T07:14:05-07:00","id":1099505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1099169#post1099169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe things like the effects of mass hysteria or mass trauma on the Dream. Or maybe something along the lines of &quot;Dreamquakes&quot; that ripple through the reality of the Dream at various times</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'll want to check out the <b>Player's Guide</b>, actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> WRT setting hacks: It's interesting, because I actually find those less useful, but that's because when I run CofD games I run them pretty &quot;straight.&quot; But <i>that's</i> because any game I run is really a de facto playtest of something, so it behooves me to use RAW as much as possible. So, hmm. Setting hacks for <b>Beast</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T08:01:54-07:00","id":1099525,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What would happen if the Kin and human relationship were flipped around? I mean, instead of Beasts feeding on humans, they feed on monsters instead. Kinship bonds are not &quot;family&quot; but &quot;preferred prey&quot; (Hunger is the &quot;collection method&quot;) - and you are what you eat. Beasts then become the predator to other predators, in a darker Hunter-like take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T08:56:26-07:00","id":1099536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1099525#post1099525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. What would happen if the Kin and human relationship were flipped around? I mean, instead of Beasts feeding on humans, they feed on monsters instead. Kinship bonds are not &quot;family&quot; but &quot;preferred prey&quot; (Hunger is the &quot;collection method&quot;) - and you are what you eat. Beasts then become the predator to other predators, in a darker Hunter-like take.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a good point. Beast feeing on Kin (or on other Beasts) is something that hasn't been addressed much so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T18:40:08-07:00","id":1099709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1099525#post1099525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. What would happen if the Kin and human relationship were flipped around? I mean, instead of Beasts feeding on humans, they feed on monsters instead. Kinship bonds are not &quot;family&quot; but &quot;preferred prey&quot; (Hunger is the &quot;collection method&quot;) - and you are what you eat. Beasts then become the predator to other predators, in a darker Hunter-like take.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Feast of Shulpae encourages you in your worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T07:35:12-07:00","id":1099818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1099536#post1099536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a good point. Beast feeing on Kin (or on other Beasts) is something that hasn't been addressed much so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it would be an interesting way of Reaching Apex. Also Possibly an Inheritance of it's own....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T10:35:45-07:00","id":1099855,"title":"","content":"In general, I'd also like to see highlighting &quot;Beasts vs Beasts&quot; conflicts.<br /> <br /> Whether it be for hunting grounds, for the same prey, or even a Beast (or a brood) feeling like another Beast or brood is going too far with their choice of feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T17:37:20-07:00","id":1099963,"title":"","content":"If setting hacks aren't good for you, a couple of interesting settings and some ideas/hooks on using them would be good. Something that gets the reader really thinking about how they can use this game?<br /> Heck, a <b><i><u>small </u></i></b>(cannot stress that enough) part of me is interested in seeing how the Begotten deal with the large crossover mess that is Chicago where the Kin knows each other already. Tokyo is actually cleaner than that and the Heroic phenomenon takes point (as it should).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T08:46:36-07:00","id":1101247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1099855#post1099855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I'd also like to see highlighting &quot;Beasts vs Beasts&quot; conflicts.<br /> <br /> Whether it be for hunting grounds, for the same prey, or even a Beast (or a brood) feeling like another Beast or brood is going too far with their choice of feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is definitely getting some ink, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T11:18:21-07:00","id":1200146,"title":"","content":"Bit of a necro but I figured this was worth revisiting now that the Player's Guide is out. Having seen all the cool new options there, does anybody have new questions they want answered? Did it check off some of the items on your hypothetical wish list?<br /> <br /> For me, I'm still hungry for more information on the interaction between Hunger, Legend, and the Beast's choice of Lessons as it relates to building their Myth. The new content on the Incarnate path was great (the Inheritances were in general) but I would still love to see more words devoted to the question of how much a Myth is something you create vs something you become. Are Horrors on the verge of Incarnating pretty much the same as they were at Lair 1 only... moreso? Or can the path there change them into something almost unrecognizably different?<br /> <br /> Also more content on Heroes, both in terms of discussion of their place in the Primordial/Bright Dream and more powers to increase their potential threat factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","user":"HelmsDerp","date":". 03-27-2018, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T15:34:20-07:00","id":1200241,"title":"","content":"I still feel like Beasts don't really have many things to do aside from &quot;Feed&quot; and &quot;Fight Heroes&quot;. They added &quot;Make a cult&quot; to the list, but cults are a thing common to a decent number of gamelines to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T19:19:41-07:00","id":1200312,"title":"","content":"More content on Heroes and Insatiables both would be great, but I'd second the idea the &quot;What does a Beast do?&quot; thing, maybe framed through the question of how broods are organized. The BPG talks about joining lairs as being this intimate experience...but like, what's the daily functioning of a brood like? What are some ways a brood could interact? One of the Demon books breaks down some approaches for how a ring could come together, and that was helpful for conceptualizing what a ring really <i>is </i>beyond &quot;a Demon-specific term for the party.&quot; So what makes a brood a <i>brood,</i> beyond the metaphysical connection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T19:42:55-07:00","id":1200318,"title":"","content":"Additionally, there's all this mentions of Beasts that &quot;explore the greater Chronicles of Darkness&quot; and its Otherworlds (Hisil, Astral Realms, Hedge, Underworld, etc)...but the materials thus far have devoted insufficiently the fluff or the crunch to fully satisfy that avenue of play. All that there is some very scattered, limited plot hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 07-08-2018, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T10:42:41-07:00","id":1233220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1200318#post1200318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, there's all this mentions of Beasts that &quot;explore the greater Chronicles of Darkness&quot; and its Otherworlds (Hisil, Astral Realms, Hedge, Underworld, etc)...but the materials thus far have devoted sufficiently the fluff or the crunch to fully satisfy that avenue of play. All that there is some very scattered, limited plot hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>While everyone has agreed on this point, I'd say tasti man says it best. Beast have great crossover potential, like how they are nightmares and changelings are fantastic dreams, yet the focus is on the daily lives beast.<br /> <br /> A storyteller guide should embrace how beast want to explore their relations to their kin, and we have that through the athaeneum faction, always discovering new things and having built vast knowledge stored in an eldritch library of lairs. Enough that mages have tried to raid it.<br /> <br /> The guardian beast could be used to explore the morality of beast. Why are they made to cause deep emotional pain to people, why are these mythic horrors attracted to them, and most importantly, what does the dark mother want from them so much as to ruin their lives and expecting obedience.<br /> <br /> Finally, while I'm short on ideas for this one, the Empusae could be used to explore beast at their most raw form, truly embracing what they are and having a very deep self understanding of themselves that the other factions can't say they have. These are the guys that see their kin and think &quot;what can I learn from them, and what can they learn from me&quot;. They may see similarities with the crone goddess and the dark mother, explore why they affect the hedge in a way the fae fear, and see similarities the primordial dream and divine fire have in heroes and disquieted mobs. Lastly, while yes, the athaeneum would also explore these, it would be in a more disconnected, academic way, with less potential than Empusae can have (which could be a reason for a team-up)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 09-15-2018, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T21:49:34-07:00","id":1306432,"title":"","content":"So, obviously the context for the original question is... radically different from when it was asked, but I have some thoughts on what I want from the BSG, and now it's time for me to get them down.<br /> <br /> 1) A Storytelling Chapter-a really good one. Above all anything else, I want it to discuss safe table practices first and foremost, followed by an ownership of the problematic elements of Beast's narrative balanced with the otherside of it (using Lessons as an example, the abusive blame game vs people who must deliver hard facts, the line between idea as control vs idea as enlightenment), practical advice how to encourage one over the other and keeping the game on point, and of course some cool means to develop cool games akin to Climbing the Ladder or Music is Always.<br /> <br /> 2) Heroes. Heroes, Heroes, <i>Heroes</i>. There's a lot of critical dialogue around Heroes that needs to be delivered on these guys, but as a general approach to how to deliver on them, a) they are <i>non-playable</i> antagonists, for a couple of reasons that should be made clear, and really just expanding on how and why Heroes are used, including a discussion of Higher integrity Heroes who fight Beasts, not to kill them for their own ego, but because they have their own Lesson Culture as concerns people but most definitely Beasts(despite be addressed in a big way, this is not a major point of this point-just very sellable) b) they need to sell tactics that create their terror before giving them powers-it's more important people know <i>how</i> to play Heroes as antagonists before we give them more toys to play with, c) Heroes need to be sold in a more individual and weird way than as a homgenous entity-to compare to Mage for a second, Heroes are less Seers and more Rapt, d) Powers that dig deeper into the imposition of Heroic narrative and the manipulation of Lair-as-psychospiritual-real-estate against Beasts, a mix of forcing things on Beasts and twisting their narratives against them, e) Heroes need <i>some</i> ability to deliver on the fact that they are the sorts who'd clean a stable out by flooding it with a river, and f) expanding their capacities as crossover antagonists-All of that in order of most important to least important.<br /> <br /> 3) Crossover-it's time to dig deeper into the hows and whys of how this work, including in no particular order a) a brief overview of the otherworlds of Hedge, Shadow, and Underworld, and an examination of reasons why Beasts'll go there and what they'll particularly face, b) a dive into how Beast interacts with the themes of other lines and visa versa, particularly with an angle of examination towards participation with, and c) how the antagonists of gamelines can factor into a Beast story and how Beast antagonists can factor into the other gamelines stories. (This idea stems from a set of essays I've been mulling over doing for some time and may still do.)<br /> <br /> 4) The Primordial Dream and Astral Realms- We got the overview and how players might utilize in the BPG, so now it's time to get into the weird and terrifying ways it can interject itself into Beast's lives-weird vertices and infections of psychospirituality, Goetia passive and invasive, more on the Insatiable, exploring the Progenitor Beasts, and utlimately the Dark Mother as a story/chronicle structure and source of antagonism as much as support.<br /> <br /> 5) Beasts, the Legends and the Myths-basically digging more into the endgames of Beasts (including but not limited to looking at Inheritances again), how the game mechanics shape the storytelling, and how Beasts work as antagonists all around.<br /> <br /> 6) Shards. I just like Shards, even if I doubt I'll ever use them. Specifically, something Chaoskampf-y, Ragnarok-y, and something more creatively sideways than I can currently think of is about what I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> 7) I would like to write for this book, please and thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T03:20:42-07:00","id":1306491,"title":"","content":"If you do get to write for it, and even if you don\u2019t, here are what I\u2019d like to have added to your points.<br /> <br /> 1) Some good discussion on those Beasts who do not believe in the lesson culture and how not teaching lessons does not equal acting foolishly on you hunger.<br /> <br /> 2) some discussion on the possibility of not having Heroes be a thing at all. With other Begotten, the Unsatiable the other supernaturals and their Antagonists and the actual Hunters we really do not actually need Heroes as extra Antagonists. Explore the themes of vulnerability that the Heroes bring to a Beast game and how it would affect things to not have them. More options are always for the better after all.<br /> <br /> 3) Don\u2019t have anything of note to add here.<br /> <br /> 4) Sounds good.<br /> <br /> 5) Again sounds good to me but perhaps some discussion on why Beasts are mortal beings with rather limited life expectansies despite their Mythic forbears having either extreme life expectansies or even being immortal or close to it. It os a rare story that has a Dragon dying of old age and they are often easily hundreds of years old, similarly Kraken is either an immortal or just so long loved it doesn\u2019t matter. Etc. Exploration of why is mortality important to themes of Beast the Primordial and how it would affect the game to have the Begotten be immortal, which would also help with crossovers as Vampire game may strecth for centuries and it would be inconvinient for the Beast player switching characters at every time skip.<br /> <br /> 6) Sounds good to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T11:52:26-07:00","id":1306597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1306491#post1306491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do get to write for it, and even if you don\u2019t, here are what I\u2019d like to have added to your points.<br /> <br /> 1) Some good discussion on those Beasts who do not believe in the lesson culture and how not teaching lessons does not equal acting foolishly on you hunger.<br /> <br /> 2) some discussion on the possibility of not having Heroes be a thing at all. With other Begotten, the Unsatiable the other supernaturals and their Antagonists and the actual Hunters we really do not actually need Heroes as extra Antagonists. Explore the themes of vulnerability that the Heroes bring to a Beast game and how it would affect things to not have them. More options are always for the better after all.<br /> <br /> 3) Don\u2019t have anything of note to add here.<br /> <br /> 4) Sounds good.<br /> <br /> 5) Again sounds good to me but perhaps some discussion on why Beasts are mortal beings with rather limited life expectansies despite their Mythic forbears having either extreme life expectansies or even being immortal or close to it. It os a rare story that has a Dragon dying of old age and they are often easily hundreds of years old, similarly Kraken is either an immortal or just so long loved it doesn\u2019t matter. Etc. Exploration of why is mortality important to themes of Beast the Primordial and how it would affect the game to have the Begotten be immortal, which would also help with crossovers as Vampire game may strecth for centuries and it would be inconvinient for the Beast player switching characters at every time skip.<br /> <br /> 6) Sounds good to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I've got some issues here.<br /> <br /> 1a) I'm really just past the point of giving a shit about non-lesson culture. Either teach or don't, decide to be meaningful or meaningless. Honestly, I still feel like enough hasn't been done <i>with</i> lesson culture and if I were going to seriously address that particular cornerstone of the Eldest family, I would actually build into more distinctive lesson cultures than not.<br /> <br /> 1b) Also, books have limited space and I'd rather use that space to make what we have work even better than trying to present options. Maybe if Beast did well enough to justify a Cults and Cultures book of Beasts, that'd be a book where I'd go and explore more of &quot;Well what the fuck do we do&quot; and various ways the Begotten answer what to do with their Hunger, but honestly, Lessons cover that fine in concept and just need to be looked at with more care and sincerity.<br /> <br /> 1c) Also, while not teaching lessons does not neccesarily equal acting foolishly, as I have pointed out in other threads, Lessons are a hell of a solid means of managing your Hunger as well as building your Lair and will reliably do so more than not teaching a lesson, and I would definitely not ignore that, again mattering for space. Honestly, a sentence akin to yours is all I need to make the point you made.<br /> <br /> 2) Nope. Heroes <i>matter. </i>They are a critical part of the dialogue at the heart of Beast the Primordial. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/850242-beast-nature-and-morality?p=851890#post851890\">I would make their role as cart upsetter clearer and the hows and whys of that starker.</a> Sure, you might not need them for every game or chronicle of Beast any more than every game of Werewolf needs an idigam, but Heroes need to have their shadows across the dialogue-even when not present, their horror lingers like the shadows of True Fae for Beasts.<br /> <br /> 3) Yep.<br /> <br /> 4) Yep.<br /> <br /> 5) I personally do not give a shit about the mortality of Beasts, nor can I reasonably find a reason that matters to the story set Beast is bringing to the table to waste time and words on mortality or immortality. There's a definite niche in there, but honestly that sounds more like an STV niche. Not everyone needs to live forever, and honestly the reincarnating Horror is a cooler angle for exploring Beast's more cyclical themes than blunt immortality (Stories gain their power through their retelling and reinvention, not their omnipresence), but even that doesn't warrant a whole lot of discussion compared to the meat and potatoes we've got on the table.<br /> <br /> 6) Yep.<br /> <br /> With a context of &quot;Beast Storyteller's Guide&quot; I'm more interested in providing the tools a storyteller needs to make a good game of Beast as it is rather than strain the word count and my stress by doing &quot;But what if we want a game that does things that Beast doesn't do?&quot; at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T12:49:17-07:00","id":1306609,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, would you also like to look into the societies beasts have such as the empusae? would you address kinship with creatures such as strix? finally, and this sounds more like a players guide thing to be honest, would explore how Life intertwines with Legend and vice versa for beast and horror","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:19:18-07:00","id":1306619,"title":"","content":"Probably not so hard? If I were going to really dive into that, I'd want to pitch an Antagonist Book in the vein of Autumn Nightmares, Pandora's Book, Predators, Book of the Deceived, and so on. I don't think we could ignore some of the societies in the discussions about Beasts and the storytelling for them, particularly covering lightly the antagonists, and I would hope to at least create one or two new models for societies, but the Beast Chapter would be more akin to the Demon chapter in the DSG, and likewise I would want to focus the crossover chapter more on how to help tell stories with the characters and societies of the protagonists.<br /> <br /> NO, outside of the DSG, what I would probably most want are a non-Night Horrors Antagonist Book and a Location Book where it makes more sense to also really dig into Cults and Cultures for Beasts. For the DSG, the goal is less &quot;here's the opposition&quot; or &quot;here's something more variable&quot; so much as &quot;here's something that will make the ST's job easier, that makes it clearer and easier to see what to do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also a Chronicler's Guide, because Mirrors-style supplements are always awesome.<br /> <br /> *I want it as a hard rule that the Dark Mother is almost always on the side of her Children, and player character Beasts in particular, so she's never an out and out antagonist unless U Dun Fuked Up, but it's worth exploring how the &quot;difference between hugging and devouring is minimal&quot; from the not supportive angle of the argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-21-2019, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:39:26-07:00","id":1306626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1306619#post1306619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not so hard? If I were going to really dive into that, I'd want to pitch an Antagonist Book in the vein of Autumn Nightmares, Pandora's Book, Predators, Book of the Deceived, and so on. I don't think we could ignore some of the societies in the discussions about Beasts and the storytelling for them, particularly covering lightly the antagonists, and I would hope to at least create one or two new models for societies, but the Beast Chapter would be more akin to the Demon chapter in the DSG, and likewise I would want to focus the crossover chapter more on how to help tell stories with the characters and societies of the protagonists.<br /> <br /> NO, outside of the DSG, what I would probably most want are a non-Night Horrors Antagonist Book and a Location Book where it makes more sense to also rally dig into Cults and Cultures for Beasts. For the DSG, the goal is less &amp;quot;here's the opposition&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;here's something more variable&amp;quot; so much as &amp;quot;here's something that will make the ST's job easier, that makes it clearer and easier to see what to do.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Also a Chronicler's Guide, because Mirrors-style supplements are always awesome.<br /> <br /> *I want it as a hard rule that the Dark Mother is almost always on the side of her Children, and player character Beasts in particular, so she's never an out and out antagonist unless U Dun Fuked Up, but it's worth exploring how the &amp;quot;difference between hugging and devouring is minimal&amp;quot; from the not supportive angle of the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks for clarifying. from every thread that has you talking about beasts, I sincerely hope you are able to be a writer for a beast storytellers guide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T13:48:57-07:00","id":1306629,"title":"","content":"On the matter of longevity: While the book isn't entirely clear if a Beast can live up to 250 years, age of Devouring + 250 years, or natural lifespan + 250 years.... that's still plenty of time for the vast majority of stories that want to have a Beast operating over time. I really can't see why we'd need significantly older ones. Vampire and Mummy do that for different but important thematic reasons. And since we already have Kinship Merits as a thing... what more needs to be said than &quot;form Kinship with something with an indefinite lifespan, and life even longer, though possibly through periods of long hibernation.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T15:02:24-07:00","id":1306652,"title":"","content":"Regarding the mortality of Beasts, I think they gain an extra decade to their Lifespan for each Lair dot above 5, extending their life span. And I think some of their Inheritances make them Immortal to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T16:59:59-07:00","id":1306678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1306652#post1306652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the mortality of Beasts, I think they gain an extra decade to their Lifespan for each Lair dot above 5, extending their life span.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's much more generous than that - every dot of Lair above 5 adds 50 years to their lifespan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T17:08:44-07:00","id":1306682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1306678#post1306678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's much more generous than that - every dot of Lair above 5 adds 50 years to their lifespan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is really generous! Lot of time there to help build yourself into the immortality of the Beast Incarnate, if that's what someone wants, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T06:24:09-07:00","id":1307736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1200241#post1200241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still feel like Beasts don't really have many things to do aside from &quot;Feed&quot; and &quot;Fight Heroes&quot;. They added &quot;Make a cult&quot; to the list, but cults are a thing common to a decent number of gamelines to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>After pondering long and hard on this question a while back, I eventually came to the conclusion that Beast is secretly a really weird slice-of-life game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T06:49:30-07:00","id":1307740,"title":"","content":"I've always found this to be a complaint common to this game (I myself have this opinion)<br /> <br /> beast works really well in both emphasizing <br /> and contrasting themes of other gamelines when in crossover. by itself it does not have much to do unless you are very good at sandbox play. personally I hope a storytellers guide is made to address this issue<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should add, beast also are very capable of bringing cokpletely new themes to games through crossover too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 04-25-2019, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:06:06-07:00","id":1307768,"title":"","content":"You don't need sandbox play to get in crossover.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the whole Apex concept exists, and why it can explicitly be something else besides one of the Begotten.<br /> <br /> The ST can just set up the game where there's an active power-struggle between different factions in another supernatural group both including potential Apexes for the area. This immediately impacts any Beasts that live there (so instant call to action rather than waiting for the PCs to decide to explore that part of the sandbox), and easily sets up a story around Kinship, politics, and helping determine the Primordial landscape of the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:06:42-07:00","id":1307769,"title":"","content":"True Facts, Beast is basically the Chronicles version of <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/118784/Golden-Sky-Stories\" target=\"_blank\">Golden Sky Stories</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:51:39-07:00","id":1307785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1079624-beast-storyteller-s-guide?p=1307768#post1307768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need sandbox play to get in crossover.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the whole Apex concept exists, and why it can explicitly be something else besides one of the Begotten.<br /> <br /> The ST can just set up the game where there's an active power-struggle between different factions in another supernatural group both including potential Apexes for the area. This immediately impacts any Beasts that live there (so instant call to action rather than waiting for the PCs to decide to explore that part of the sandbox), and easily sets up a story around Kinship, politics, and helping determine the Primordial landscape of the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt say it needed to be a sandbox for crossover. I stated that it is a game that works best through sandbox play than the other gamelines (though, I did originally say you NEED a group who is good with sandbox style play to play a beast only game, which is not true)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T22:16:54-07:00","id":1309574,"title":"","content":"I don't have a good place to put this, and it seems a bit much to make a thread, so here goes stuff I just want down.<br /> <br /> &quot;A god is just a monster you kneel to.&quot;-Michael Voght, Fall of Gods<br /> <br /> &quot;I ask of thee-art thou mankind?&quot;&quot;Nay! I am the world-the world inside the gourd.&quot;-Gakuto Mikumo, The Mystic Archives of Dantalion<br /> <br /> &quot;Mercy and compassion are virtues that only the strong are privileged to possess. And I am strong.&quot;-Ryohgo Narita, Baccano!<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'm an existence called &quot;evil&quot; now. And if evil is supposed to disrupt the divine and be a force of chaos, it's only natural for me to upset the laws of a god.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-13-2019, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}